<title>UK: C&amp;W gains in cable merger aftermath.</title>
<headline>C&amp;W gains in cable merger aftermath.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cable and Wireless advanced 12 pence to 488, gaining extra momentum following positive comments in the Sunday newspapers on last week's news of its cable tv merger in Britain.</p>
<p>&quot;The press comments over the weekend helped,&quot; said one dealer, pointing to an article in the Sunday Times which said the link-up created a powerful new force in the cable industry.</p>
<p>The deal, announced last Tuesday, brings together the British operations of Cable and Wireless, NYNEX of the U.S. and Bell Canada International, to eclipse Telewest as the biggest cable television operator in the UK.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
